2025-03-27T23:54:00 NOTE
2025-03-27T23:54:00 
2025-03-27T23:54:00 There have been some changes starting with 3.2 regarding where and how libnl
2025-03-27T23:54:00 is being installed on the system in order to allow multiple libnl versions
2025-03-27T23:54:00 to be installed in parallel:
2025-03-27T23:54:00 
2025-03-27T23:54:00 - Headers will be installed in ${prefix}/include/libnl3, therefore
2025-03-27T23:54:00 you will need to add "-I/usr/include/libnl3" to CFLAGS
2025-03-27T23:54:00 
2025-03-27T23:54:00 - The library basename was renamed to libnl-3, i.e. the SO names become
2025-03-27T23:54:00 libnl-3.so., libnl-route-3.so, etc.
2025-03-27T23:54:00 
2025-03-27T23:54:00 - libtool versioning was assumed, to ease detection of compatible library
2025-03-27T23:54:00 versions.
2025-03-27T23:54:00 
2025-03-27T23:54:00 If you are using pkg-config for detecting and linking against the library
2025-03-27T23:54:00 things will continue magically as if nothing every happened. If you are
2025-03-27T23:54:00 linking manually you need to adapt your Makefiles or switch to using
2025-03-27T23:54:00 pkg-config files.
2025-03-27T23:54:00 
